.Dd July 9, 2026
.Dt RETICULUM-GO 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm reticulum-go
.Nd Reticulum network daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Cm daemon
.Sh DESCRIPTION
When started with no subcommand (or with
.Cm daemon ) ,
.Nm
runs the Reticulum network stack: interfaces from configuration, transport,
shared-instance RPC, optional control API, and optional sandbox.
.Pp
Configuration is loaded from
.Pa ~/.reticulum-go/config .
On first run a default config is created if missing.
.Pp
On Unix, SIGHUP reloads interface configuration where supported.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGINT , SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown.
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload interfaces from configuration (Unix).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.reticulum-go/storage/"
.It Pa ~/.reticulum-go/config
Daemon configuration.
.It Pa ~/.reticulum-go/storage/
Persistent state.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr reticulum-go 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Quad4.io
